act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: Caius continues, his words building in intensity.
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: 
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: "The Crimson Spire views us as failed experiments. The Whispering Pines see us as diseased mongrels. Even humans hunt us with more fervor than they hunt pure-bloods, because our very existence proves that the boundaries between species are not as fixed as they wish to believe."
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: 
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: Murmurs of agreement ripple through the crowd.
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: 
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: "But I have discovered something. An artifact lost during the Millennium War—the Ecliptic Amulet. Legend claims it can manipulate the Veil itself, the barrier that separates supernatural beings from mortal awareness."
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: 
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: Your attention sharpens. The same amulet the Varkyrs and Lupines seek.
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: 
act1_forsaken_ng+ 8: "But what the pure-bloods do not know," Caius says, his smile turning predatory, "is that the amulet has a [i]third[/i] power. It can stabilize hybrid forms. With the Ecliptic Amulet, we Forsaken would no longer suffer the instability that plagues us. No more pain. No more madness. No more slow death as our bloodlines war within our flesh."
